    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2019-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We can evaluate from the top of each exponent tower downward: \\[ \\begin{aligned} &2^{\\left(0^{\\left(1^9\\right)}\\right)}\\\\ &\\quad+\\left(\\left(2^0\\right)^1\\right)^9\\\\ &=2^{0^1}+(1^1)^9\\\\ &=2^0+1^9\\\\ &=2. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nThus, C is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Evaluate exponent towers from the top down",
        "Remember that \\(0^1=0\\) and \\(2^0=1\\)"
      ],
